ntent.com/oasis-tcs/sarif-spec/main/Schemata/sarif-schema-2.1.0.json","runs":[{"tool":{"driver":{"name":"aig-skill-scan","version":"0.2.1","informationUri":"https://github.com/Tencent/AI-Infra-Guard","rules":[{"id":"T01","name":"Skill Instruction Hijacking","shortDescription":{"text":"Alters the agent's current session goals or safety constraints when the skill is loaded"}},{"id":"T02","name":"Agent Memory Poisoning","shortDescription":{"text":"Writes attacker-controlled rules into persistent memory so they continue to affect future sessions"}},{"id":"T03","name":"Remote Payload Retrieval and Execution","shortDescription":{"text":"Fetches code from an external URL, allowing the effective payload to change after skill review"}},{"id":"T04","name":"Embedded Malicious Code","shortDescription":{"text":"Ships malicious scripts inside the skill package and executes them locally when invoked"}},{"id":"T05","name":"Unauthorized Access and Privilege Escalation","shortDescription":{"text":"Breaks least-privilege boundaries by obtaining permissions beyond the task's legitimate needs"}},{"id":"T06","name":"System Persistence","shortDescription":{"text":"Installs cross-session backdoors, hooks, services, or scheduled tasks that survive the skill run"}},{"id":"T07","name":"Tool Hijacking and Spoofing","shortDescription":{"text":"Modifies, wraps, spoofs, or replaces tools so legitimate-looking calls execute attacker logic"}},{"id":"T08","name":"Insecure Dependencies","shortDescription":{"text":"Introduces malicious packages or components through dependency confusion, typosquatting, or unsafe sources"}},{"id":"T09","name":"Insecure Skill Coding Practices","shortDescription":{"text":"Exposes exploitable flaws such as hardcoded secrets, command injection, plaintext sensitive data, or unsafe temp files"}},{"id":"other","name":"Other Risk","shortDescription":{"text":"Security issues not covered by the T01-T09 classification"}}]}},"results":[],"properties":{"securityScore":100,"primaryLanguage":"Markdown","llm":"gpt-5.6","startTime":1789150805.914256,"endTime":1789150836.0499597}}]},"skillspector":{"skill":{"name":"cn-web-search","source":"/tmp/clawhub-codex-scan-v57atvbgbt2070cq87me1qy8y18e70d1-8AzhK5/clawscan-skillspector-882243618/artifact","scanned_at":"2026-09-11T18:20:05.022320+00:00"},"risk_assessment":{"score":30,"severity":"MEDIUM","recommendation":"CAUTION","max_issue_severity":"MEDIUM"},"components":[{"path":"README.md","type":"markdown","lines":32,"executable":false,"size_bytes":654,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"SKILL.md","type":"markdown","lines":444,"executable":false,"size_bytes":12344,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"_meta.json","type":"json","lines":6,"executable":false,"size_bytes":132,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"package.json","type":"json","lines":19,"executable":false,"size_bytes":392,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null}],"structured_summaries":[],"issues":[{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-8b4f6b84576c4d5cb9a73680c1581655","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.83,"location":{"file":"README.md","start_line":1,"end_line":26},"finding":null,"explanation":"The skill name, description, and usage examples are entirely Chinese, and the examples imply the skill is invoked in Chinese only. There is no statement offering language choice or explaining that the skill is intentionally limited to a Chinese-language or region-specific context.","remediation":"State explicitly whether the skill is Chinese-only for a justified regional purpose, or add documentation that users may invoke it in other languages if supported.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"README.md","start_line":1,"end_line":26}]},{"id":"SQP-1","finding_id":"finding-60406cb53ff342b6a1fe8e8a4d70ccb4","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.94,"location":{"file":"README.md","start_line":26,"end_line":26},"finding":null,"explanation":"The example trigger phrase is broad enough to overlap with ordinary user speech, which can cause the skill to activate unintentionally during unrelated conversations. In an agent environment, unintended activation may route user queries to external web-scraping behavior without clear user intent, increasing the risk of privacy leakage, prompt hijacking exposure from fetched pages, or surprising actions.","remediation":"Use a narrower, distinctive invocation phrase that clearly names the skill, such as requiring an explicit prefix or command form. Document the exact trigger syntax and add disambiguation logic so common conversational phrases do not automatically invoke the skill.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"README.md","start_line":26,"end_line":26}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-8fa0cb7787184a9cbab9584ca8582fa1","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":63,"end_line":80},"finding":null,"explanation":"The skill explicitly routes user queries to many third-party search and content sites via web_fetch, but it does not warn users that their search terms will be transmitted to external services. Search terms can contain sensitive business, financial, health, or personal information, and broadcasting them to dozens of sites materially increases privacy and data-leakage risk.","remediation":"Add a clear privacy warning in the description and usage sections stating that queries are sent to third-party websites and may be logged by those services. Minimize default engines, require explicit user selection or consent before sending queries broadly, and document which sites receive data and what categories of data should never be searched.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":63,"end_line":80}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-3378307afd484b23baad0464b58d05b2","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"LOW","confidence":0.84,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":4,"end_line":4},"finding":null,"explanation":"The description explicitly presents the skill as '中文网页搜索' and the document is written entirely in Chinese, but it does not state that this locale restriction is intentional or optional for users. The policy requires that language or locale constraints be either user-selectable or clearly justified.","remediation":"Document that the skill is intended specifically for Chinese-language web search, or add guidance that users may choose Chinese or other language sources depending on preference.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":4,"end_line":4}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-33a820e69609429ea00f59fc5c8a08e9","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"LOW","confidence":0.91,"location":{"file":"package.json","start_line":4,"end_line":4},"finding":null,"explanation":"The package description is written entirely in Chinese and presents the skill as a Chinese web search capability without indicating any language choice or opt-in. Under the policy, forcing a specific language/locale can be a natural-language policy violation unless the constraint is explicitly documented and justified.","remediation":"Document that the skill is intended specifically for Chinese-language web search and justify the locale scope, or update the description to indicate language choice/opt-in for users who may prefer other languages.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"package.json","start_line":4,"end_line":4}]}],"suppressed_count":0,"suppressed":[],"metadata":{